# GitHub operations

- Repository identity is byShadow64/tg-proxy. Preserve upstream attribution and licenses.
- Do not import old private Git refs/history or move existing tags.
- Use connected tools or normal Git/Desktop authorization; never extract another tool's secrets.
- Keep changes reviewable and preserve unrelated work. No force push or protection bypass.
- Use bounded pagination, checkpoints and conditional requests where supported.
- Respect Retry-After/Reset and secondary backoff; do not rotate tokens/IPs to evade limits.
- Related mutations are sequential, at least one second apart in a series.
- After uncertain POST/dispatch, inspect remote state before retrying.
- Read access and404 do not establish write permission or the reason for an account restriction.
- Wiki, Pages and source docs are different surfaces; do not claim deployment from a docs edit.
- Access/security/domain settings require an explicit owner instruction.
- Public download/release-page links are prohibited; follow docs/GITHUB_CONTENT_POLICY.md.
